IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 6 -- Amendment and repeal of Acts (ss 17A to 22C).
-- Section 18 and section 22C(1) fix times and are in qld-interpretation-time.l4.
-- Each rule here takes the facts of an Act or provision as plain yes or no inputs and answers what the section says follows.

§ `Part 6 -- Amendment and repeal of Acts`

§§ `s 17A -- Act may be amended or repealed in same parliamentary session`

-- src:282 | An Act may be amended or repealed in the session of Parliament in which it is passed.
@ref s 17A (src:282-282)
GIVEN `it is in the session of Parliament in which the Act is passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Act may be amended or repealed (s 17A)` IS
    IF `it is in the session of Parliament in which the Act is passed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 19 -- Repealed and amended Acts not revived`

-- src:289 | (1) In this section—
-- src:290 | Act includes a provision of an Act.
@ref s 19(1), definition Act (src:289-290)
GIVEN `the thing is a provision of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a provision of an Act is an Act in s 19 (s 19(1), definition Act)` IS
    IF `the thing is a provision of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:291 | repeal includes expiry.
@ref s 19(1), definition repeal (src:291-291)
GIVEN `the event is the expiry of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `expiry is a repeal in s 19 (s 19(1), definition repeal)` IS
    IF `the event is the expiry of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): if the first Act is repealed by the other Act, the first Act is not revived merely because the other Act is repealed.
-- src:292 | (2) If an Act (the first Act) is repealed by another Act (the other Act), the first Act is not revived merely because the other Act is repealed.
@ref s 19(2) (src:292-292)
GIVEN `the first Act is repealed by the other Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other Act is repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first Act is revived merely because the other Act is repealed (s 19(2))` IS
    IF `the first Act is repealed by the other Act` AND `the other Act is repealed` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- (3): if the first Act is amended by the other Act, the continuing operation of the amendments is not affected merely because the other Act is repealed,
-- and the first Act is not revived in its form before the amendments took effect merely because of the repeal.
-- src:296 | (3) If an Act (the first Act) is amended by another Act (the other Act), the continuing operation of the amendments made by the other Act is not affected merely because the other Act is repealed and, in particular, the first Act is not revived in the form that it was in before the amendments took effect merely because of the repeal.
@ref s 19(3) (src:296-296)
GIVEN `the first Act is amended by the other Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other Act is repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the continuing operation of the amendments is affected merely because the other Act is repealed (s 19(3))` IS
    IF `the first Act is amended by the other Act` AND `the other Act is repealed` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:296 | (3) If an Act (the first Act) is amended by another Act (the other Act), the continuing operation of the amendments made by the other Act is not affected merely because the other Act is repealed and, in particular, the first Act is not revived in the form that it was in before the amendments took effect merely because of the repeal.
@ref s 19(3) (src:296-296)
GIVEN `the first Act is amended by the other Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other Act is repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first Act is revived in the form it was in before the amendments took effect merely because of the repeal (s 19(3))` IS
    IF `the first Act is amended by the other Act` AND `the other Act is repealed` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:300 | (4) This section is in addition to, and does not limit, sections 20 and 20A, or any provision of the law by which the repeal is made.
@ref s 19(4) (src:300-300)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19 limits s 20, s 20A or any provision of the law by which the repeal is made (s 19(4))` IS FALSE

§§ `s 19A -- Commencement not undone if omitted`

-- src:302 | If a provision of an Act provides for the commencement of a law and the law has commenced, the later omission of the provision does not affect the continuing operation of the law.
@ref s 19A (src:302-302)
GIVEN `a provision of an Act provides for the commencement of a law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law has commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is later omitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the later omission of the provision affects the continuing operation of the law (s 19A)` IS
    IF `a provision of an Act provides for the commencement of a law` AND `the law has commenced` AND `the provision is later omitted` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 20 -- Saving of operation of repealed Act etc.`

-- src:304 | (1) In this section—
-- src:305 | Act includes a provision of an Act.
@ref s 20(1), definition Act (src:304-305)
GIVEN `the thing is a provision of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a provision of an Act is an Act in s 20 (s 20(1), definition Act)` IS
    IF `the thing is a provision of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:306 | repeal includes expiry.
@ref s 20(1), definition repeal (src:306-306)
GIVEN `the event is the expiry of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `expiry is a repeal in s 20 (s 20(1), definition repeal)` IS
    IF `the event is the expiry of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Thing a repeal or amendment of an Act may touch` IS ONE OF
    `anything not in force or existing at the time the repeal or amendment takes effect`
    `the previous operation of the Act or anything suffered, done or begun under the Act`
    `a right, privilege or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the Act`
    `a penalty incurred in relation to an offence arising under the Act`
    `an investigation, proceeding or remedy in relation to a right, privilege, liability or penalty mentioned in s 20(2)(c) or (d)`
    `the proof of anything that has happened`
    `any right, privilege or liability saved by the operation of the Act`
    `any repeal or amendment made by the Act`
    `any savings, transitional or validating effect of the Act`
    `anything else`

-- (2) says the repeal or amendment "does not" revive (a) or affect (b) to (e); (4) says without limiting (2) and (3) it does not affect (a) to (d).
-- Nine named things: a flat negative (JUST FALSE).  Any other thing is not addressed (NOTHING).
-- src:307 | (2) The repeal or amendment of an Act does not—
-- src:308 | (a) revive anything not in force or existing at the time the repeal or amendment takes effect; or
-- src:309 | (b) affect the previous operation of the Act or anything suffered, done or begun under the Act; or
-- src:310 | (c) affect a right, privilege or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the Act; or
-- src:311 | (d) affect a penalty incurred in relation to an offence arising under the Act; or
-- src:312 | (e) affect an investigation, proceeding or remedy in relation to a right, privilege, liability or penalty mentioned in paragraph (c) or (d).
@ref s 20(2) (src:307-312)
-- src:314 | (4) Without limiting subsections (2) and (3), the repeal or amendment of an Act does not affect—
-- src:315 | (a) the proof of anything that has happened; or
-- src:316 | (b) any right, privilege or liability saved by the operation of the Act; or
-- src:317 | (c) any repeal or amendment made by the Act; or
-- src:318 | (d) any savings, transitional or validating effect of the Act.
@ref s 20(4) (src:314-318)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing a repeal or amendment of an Act may touch`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the repeal or amendment of an Act revives or affects the thing (s 20(2) and (4))` IS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `anything else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Step taken in relation to a repealed or amended Act` IS ONE OF
    `the investigation, proceeding or remedy is started`
    `the investigation, proceeding or remedy is continued`
    `the investigation, proceeding or remedy is completed`
    `the right, privilege or liability is enforced`
    `the penalty is imposed`
    `any other step`

-- src:313 | (3) The investigation, proceeding or remedy may be started, continued or completed, and the right, privilege or liability may be enforced and the penalty imposed, as if the repeal or amendment had not happened.
@ref s 20(3) (src:313-313)
GIVEN step IS A `Step taken in relation to a repealed or amended Act`
      `it relates to a right, privilege, liability or penalty mentioned in s 20(2)(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the step may be taken as if the repeal or amendment had not happened (s 20(3))` IS
    IF NOT `it relates to a right, privilege, liability or penalty mentioned in s 20(2)(c) or (d)`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER step
        WHEN `any other step` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:319 | (5) This section is in addition to, and does not limit, sections 19 and 20A, or any provision of the law by which the repeal or amendment is made.
@ref s 20(5) (src:319-319)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20 limits s 19, s 20A or any provision of the law by which the repeal or amendment is made (s 20(5))` IS FALSE

§§ `s 20A -- Repeal does not end saving, transitional or validating effect etc.`

-- src:321 | (1) In this section—
-- src:322 | Act includes a provision of an Act.
@ref s 20A(1), definition Act (src:321-322)
GIVEN `the thing is a provision of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a provision of an Act is an Act in s 20A (s 20A(1), definition Act)` IS
    IF `the thing is a provision of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:323 | repeal includes expiry.
@ref s 20A(1), definition repeal (src:323-323)
GIVEN `the event is the expiry of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `expiry is a repeal in s 20A (s 20A(1), definition repeal)` IS
    IF `the event is the expiry of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of declaring or validating provision` IS ONE OF
    `declares a thing for a saving or transitional purpose (whether or not the Act is expressed to be made for a purpose of that type)`
    `validates a thing that may otherwise be invalid`
    `declares a thing for a purpose that is consequential on a declaration mentioned in paragraph (a) or a validation mentioned in paragraph (b) (whether or not the Act is expressed to be made for a purpose of that type)`
    `none of these`

-- src:324 | (2) If an Act—
-- src:325 | (a) declares a thing for a saving or transitional purpose (whether or not the Act is expressed to be made for a purpose of that type); or
-- src:326 | (b) validates a thing that may otherwise be invalid; or
-- src:327 | (c) declares a thing for a purpose that is consequential on a declaration mentioned in paragraph (a) or a validation mentioned in paragraph (b) (whether or not the Act is expressed to be made for a purpose of that type);
-- src:328 | the declaratory or validating effect of the Act does not end merely because of the repeal of the Act.
@ref s 20A(2) (src:324-328)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of declaring or validating provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the declaratory or validating effect of the Act ends merely because of the repeal of the Act (s 20A(2))` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `none of these` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Law in s 20A(3)` IS ONE OF
    `the declared law`
    `the savings law`

-- src:336 | (3) If an Act (the savings law) declares an Act (the declared law) to be a law to which this section applies—
-- src:337 | (a) the effect of the declared law does not end merely because of its repeal; and
-- src:338 | (b) the effect of the savings law does not end merely because of its repeal.
@ref s 20A(3) (src:336-338)
GIVEN law IS A `Law in s 20A(3)`
      `the savings law declares the declared law to be a law to which s 20A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the effect of the law ends merely because of its repeal (s 20A(3))` IS
    IF `the savings law declares the declared law to be a law to which s 20A applies` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:339 | (4) A declaration may be made for subsection (3) about an Act whether or not the Act is a law to which subsection (2) applies.
@ref s 20A(4) (src:339-339)
GIVEN `the Act is a law to which subsection (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a declaration may be made for s 20A(3) about the Act (s 20A(4))` IS JUST TRUE

-- src:340 | (5) A declaration made for subsection (3) about an Act does not imply that, in the absence of a declaration about it, another Act is not a law to which this section applies.
@ref s 20A(5) (src:340-340)
GIVEN `a declaration made for subsection (3) about an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the declaration implies that, in the absence of a declaration, another Act is not a law to which s 20A applies (s 20A(5))` IS
    IF `a declaration made for subsection (3) about an Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:341 | (6) This section is in addition to, and does not limit, sections 19 and 20, or any provision of the law by which the repeal is made.
@ref s 20A(6) (src:341-341)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20A limits s 19, s 20 or any provision of the law by which the repeal is made (s 20A(6))` IS FALSE

§§ `s 20B -- Continuance of appointments etc. made under amended provisions`

-- (1): applies if (a) a provision of a law expressly or impliedly authorises or requires an appointment, a delegation, or the doing of anything else (other than making a statutory instrument);
-- (b) the provision is amended by an Act; and (c) under the amended provision the appointment may be made, the function or power delegated, or the thing done.
-- src:343 | (1) This section applies if—
-- src:344 | (a) a provision of a law expressly or impliedly authorises or requires—
-- src:345 | (i) the making of an appointment; or
-- src:346 | (ii) the delegation of a function or power; or
-- src:347 | (iii) the doing of anything else (other than the making of a statutory instrument); and
-- src:348 | (b) the provision is amended by an Act; and
-- src:349 | (c) under the amended provision—
-- src:350 | (i) the appointment may be made; or
-- src:351 | (ii) the function or power may be delegated; or
-- src:352 | (iii) the thing may be done.
@ref s 20B(1) (src:343-352)
GIVEN `a provision of a law expressly or impliedly authorises or requires the making of an appointment, the delegation of a function or power, or the doing of anything else (other than the making of a statutory instrument)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is amended by an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the amended provision the appointment may be made, the function or power may be delegated, or the thing may be done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20B applies (s 20B(1))` IS
    IF    `a provision of a law expressly or impliedly authorises or requires the making of an appointment, the delegation of a function or power, or the doing of anything else (other than the making of a statutory instrument)`
       AND `the provision is amended by an Act`
       AND `under the amended provision the appointment may be made, the function or power may be delegated, or the thing may be done`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:353 | (2) An appointment, delegation or other thing mentioned in subsection (1) that was in force immediately before the commencement of the amendment continues to have effect after the commencement as if it had been done under the amended provision.
@ref s 20B(2) (src:353-353)
GIVEN `s 20B applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment, delegation or other thing was in force immediately before the commencement of the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment, delegation or other thing continues to have effect after the commencement as if it had been done under the amended provision (s 20B(2))` IS
    IF `s 20B applies` AND `the appointment, delegation or other thing was in force immediately before the commencement of the amendment` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of change to a provision` IS ONE OF
    `an amendment in the ordinary sense`
    `omission and re-enactment in the same law (with or without modification)`
    `omission and re-enactment in another law`
    `any other change`

-- (3): amend includes omit and re-enact in the same law, but does not include omit and re-enact in another law.
-- src:354 | (3) In this section—
-- src:355 | amend includes omit and re-enact in the same law (with or without modification), but does not include omit and re-enact in another law.
@ref s 20B(3) (src:354-355)
GIVEN change IS A `Kind of change to a provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change is an amendment in s 20B (s 20B(3), definition amend)` IS
    CONSIDER change
    WHEN `an amendment in the ordinary sense` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `omission and re-enactment in the same law (with or without modification)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `omission and re-enactment in another law` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `any other change` THEN NOTHING

§§ `s 20C -- Creation of offences and changes in penalties`

-- src:357 | (1) In this section—
-- src:358 | Act includes a provision of an Act.
@ref s 20C(1), definition Act (src:357-358)
GIVEN `the thing is a provision of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a provision of an Act is an Act in s 20C (s 20C(1), definition Act)` IS
    IF `the thing is a provision of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): if an Act makes an act or omission an offence, it is only an offence if committed after the Act commences.
-- src:359 | (2) If an Act makes an act or omission an offence, the act or omission is only an offence if committed after the Act commences.
@ref s 20C(2) (src:359-359)
GIVEN `the Act makes the act or omission an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission was committed after the Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act or omission is an offence under the Act (s 20C(2))` IS
    IF NOT `the Act makes the act or omission an offence`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the act or omission was committed after the Act commenced`

-- src:360 | (3) If an Act increases the maximum or minimum penalty, or the penalty, for an offence, the increase applies only to an offence committed after the Act commences.
@ref s 20C(3) (src:360-360)
GIVEN `the Act increases the maximum or minimum penalty, or the penalty, for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence was committed after the Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the increase applies to the offence (s 20C(3))` IS
    IF NOT `the Act increases the maximum or minimum penalty, or the penalty, for an offence`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the offence was committed after the Act commenced`

§§ `ss 21 and 22 -- continuance of repealed provisions, Acts read as one`

-- s 21: the repealed provisions continue in force until the new provisions commence.  The period is fixed by the text: after commencement, JUST FALSE.
-- src:362 | If an Act repeals some or all of the provisions of an Act and enacts new provisions in substitution for the repealed provisions, the repealed provisions continue in force until the new provisions commence.
@ref s 21 (src:362-362)
GIVEN `an Act repeals some or all of the provisions of an Act and enacts new provisions in substitution for the repealed provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new provisions have commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the repealed provisions continue in force (s 21)` IS
    IF `an Act repeals some or all of the provisions of an Act and enacts new provisions in substitution for the repealed provisions`
    THEN JUST (NOT `the new provisions have commenced`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:364 | An Act and all Acts amending the Act are to be read as one.
@ref s 22 (src:364-364)
GIVEN `the other Act amends the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Act and an Act amending it are to be read as one (s 22)` IS
    IF `the other Act amends the Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 22A and 22B -- insertion of provisions, how an amendment is made`

DECLARE `Kind of thing inserted by an amending Act` IS ONE OF
    `a subsection`
    `a paragraph`
    `a subparagraph`
    `a sub-subparagraph`
    `a definition`
    `another provision`
    `an example, note or penalty`

DECLARE `Position of insertion` IS ONE OF
    `the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position`
    `the appropriate alphabetical position`
    `the appropriate alphabetical position, determined on a letter-by-letter basis`
    `the end of the provision`

-- (1) to (7): where the Act does not specify the position.  Subsections, subparagraphs and other provisions in a series: numerical or alphanumerical;
-- paragraphs and sub-subparagraphs: alphabetical; definitions: alphabetical, letter-by-letter; examples, notes and penalties: the end of the provision.
-- (1) to (6) apply to a thing "that is to form part of a series"; (7) has no such condition.
-- src:366 | (1) If an Act amends a provision of a law by inserting a subsection that is to form part of a series of subsections, and does not specify the position in the provision where it is to be inserted, the subsection is to be inserted in the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position.
@ref s 22A(1) (src:366-366)
-- src:367 | (2) If an Act amends a provision of a law by inserting a paragraph that is to form part of a series of paragraphs, and does not specify the position in the provision where it is to be inserted, the paragraph is to be inserted in the appropriate alphabetical position.
@ref s 22A(2) (src:367-367)
-- src:368 | (3) If an Act amends a provision of a law by inserting a subparagraph that is to form part of a series of subparagraphs, and does not specify the position in the provision where it is to be inserted, the subparagraph is to be inserted in the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position.
@ref s 22A(3) (src:368-368)
-- src:369 | (4) If an Act amends a provision of a law by inserting a sub-subparagraph that is to form part of a series of sub-subparagraphs, and does not specify the position in the provision where it is to be inserted, the sub-subparagraph is to be inserted in the appropriate alphabetical position.
@ref s 22A(4) (src:369-369)
-- src:370 | (5) If an Act amends a provision of a law by inserting a definition that is to form part of a series of definitions, and does not specify the position in the provision where it is to be inserted, the definition is to be inserted in the appropriate alphabetical position, determined on a letter-by-letter basis.
@ref s 22A(5) (src:370-370)
-- src:371 | (6) If an Act otherwise amends a provision of a law by inserting a provision that is to form part of a series of provisions, and does not specify the position in the first provision where it is to be inserted, the second provision is to be inserted in the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position.
@ref s 22A(6) (src:371-371)
-- src:372 | (7) If an Act amends a provision of a law by inserting an example, note or penalty, and does not specify the position in the provision where it is to be inserted, the example, note or penalty is to be inserted at the end of the provision.
@ref s 22A(7) (src:372-372)
GIVEN thing IS A `Kind of thing inserted by an amending Act`
      `the thing is to form part of a series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act specifies the position in the provision where it is to be inserted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Position of insertion`
DECIDE `where the thing is to be inserted (s 22A)` IS
    IF `the Act specifies the position in the provision where it is to be inserted`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `an example, note or penalty` THEN JUST `the end of the provision`
        WHEN `a subsection` THEN IF `the thing is to form part of a series` THEN JUST `the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position` ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `a paragraph` THEN IF `the thing is to form part of a series` THEN JUST `the appropriate alphabetical position` ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `a subparagraph` THEN IF `the thing is to form part of a series` THEN JUST `the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position` ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `a sub-subparagraph` THEN IF `the thing is to form part of a series` THEN JUST `the appropriate alphabetical position` ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `a definition` THEN IF `the thing is to form part of a series` THEN JUST `the appropriate alphabetical position, determined on a letter-by-letter basis` ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `another provision` THEN IF `the thing is to form part of a series` THEN JUST `the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:373 | (8) In determining the appropriate position in which a provision is to be inserted, regard may be had to current Queensland legislative drafting practice.
@ref s 22A(8) (src:373-373)
GIVEN `the appropriate position in which a provision is to be inserted is being determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `regard may be had to current Queensland legislative drafting practice (s 22A(8))` IS
    IF `the appropriate position in which a provision is to be inserted is being determined` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of amendment to a word` IS ONE OF
    `omitting a word`
    `omitting a word and inserting another word`
    `inserting a word before or after a particular word`
    `any other amendment`

-- src:375 | If an Act amends a provision of a law—
-- src:376 | (a) by omitting a word; or
-- src:377 | (b) by omitting a word and inserting another word; or
-- src:378 | (c) by inserting a word before or after a particular word;
-- src:379 | the amendment is to be made wherever possible in the provision.
@ref s 22B (src:375-379)
GIVEN amendment IS A `Kind of amendment to a word`
      `the amendment is possible at the place in the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the amendment is to be made at the place in the provision (s 22B)` IS
    CONSIDER amendment
    WHEN `any other amendment` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF `the amendment is possible at the place in the provision` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 22C -- Automatic repeal of amending Act (subsections (2) to (4))`

-- src:382 | (2) A repeal under subsection (1) has effect for all purposes, including, for example, sections 19 to 20A.
@ref s 22C(2) (src:382-382)
GIVEN `the repeal is under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a repeal under s 22C(1) has effect for all purposes, including ss 19 to 20A (s 22C(2))` IS
    IF `the repeal is under subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:383 | (3) This section is in addition to, and does not limit the operation of, any other provision of this Act about repeals.
@ref s 22C(3) (src:383-383)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22C limits the operation of any other provision of this Act about repeals (s 22C(3))` IS FALSE

DECLARE `Kind of provision in an Act` IS ONE OF
    `the Act's long title`
    `the Act's preamble`
    `a provision about the Act's citation`
    `a provision about the Act's commencement`
    `a provision providing for the amendment or repeal of an Act or other instrument (including a provision identifying the amended or repealed instrument)`
    `a provision providing for the extension of the period before commencement, under section 15DA(2), of an Act or a provision of an Act that has not commenced within 1 year of the assent day`
    `a provision declaring an Act or a provision of an Act to be a law to which section 20A applies`
    `any other provision`

-- "amending Act means an Act that consists only of provisions of the following types": "only" closes the list.
-- src:385 | amending Act means an Act that consists only of provisions of the following types—
-- src:386 | (a) the Act’s long title;
-- src:387 | (b) the Act’s preamble (if any);
-- src:388 | (c) a provision about the Act’s citation;
-- src:389 | (d) a provision (if any) about the Act’s commencement;
-- src:390 | (e) a provision providing for the amendment or repeal of an Act or other instrument (including a provision identifying the amended or repealed instrument);
-- src:391 | (f) a provision providing for the extension of the period before commencement, under section 15DA(2), of an Act or a provision of an Act that has not commenced within 1 year of the assent day;
-- src:392 | (g) a provision declaring an Act or a provision of an Act to be a law to which section 20A applies.
@ref s 22C(4), definition amending Act (src:385-392)
GIVEN `the kinds of provision the Act contains` IS A LIST OF `Kind of provision in an Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an Act is an amending Act (s 22C(4), definition amending Act)` IS
    JUST (NOT (elem `any other provision` `the kinds of provision the Act contains`))

-- src:404 | assent day means the date of assent of—
-- src:405 | (a) if the provision provides for the extension of the period before commencement, under section 15DA(2), of an Act—the Act; or
-- src:406 | (b) if the provision provides for the extension of the period before commencement, under section 15DA(2), of a provision of an Act—the Act that enacts the provision.
@ref s 22C(4), definition assent day (src:404-406)
GIVEN `the provision extends the period before commencement of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of assent of the Act` IS A DATE
      `the date of assent of the Act that enacts the provision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the assent day in s 22C (s 22C(4), definition assent day)` IS
    IF `the provision extends the period before commencement of an Act` THEN `the date of assent of the Act` ELSE `the date of assent of the Act that enacts the provision`
